(Analysis) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I calculated the average period for each length and then squared it. I plotted T² against) Tj T*
(L and drew a line of best fit. The gradient of the line was 4.12 s² m-¹. Using g =) Tj T*
(4pi²/gradient I got g = 9.5821 m s-².) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Conclusion) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The experiment proves that the period of a pendulum depends on its length and that g =) Tj T*
(9.5821 m s-². This is close to the real value. The results were as expected.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Evaluation) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There were some errors in the experiment. Human error and reaction time affected the) Tj T*
(results. The equipment was not very accurate. To improve the experiment I would use better) Tj T*
(equipment and do more trials.) Tj T*
